config-connector-extensions patch 0015: mockgcp keeps a deleted Cloud SQL backup run, with status DELETED, as the real API does.

Written here, on upstream's mocksql/sqlbackupruns.go (on master since
2026-11-18; until then patch 0003 carried PR #12553's mock), for
sqladmin.gcp.hfl.dev SQLAdminBackup. A live run against a real project
(docs/live-runs.md, 2026-11-09) showed that after backupRuns.delete
completes, backupRuns.get still returns the run with status DELETED rather
than 404; upstream's mock removes it. Now backupRuns.delete marks the run
DELETED and keeps it. Deleting a run already DELETED answers 404 (not seen
live; the simplest choice).

Upstream candidate: yes; upstream's mock assumes a deleted run is gone.
diff --git a/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackupruns.go b/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackupruns.go
index 7f23737cb..e04425764 100644
--- a/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackupruns.go
+++ b/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackupruns.go
@@ -130,7 +130,14 @@ func (s *sqlBackupRunsServer) Delete(ctx context.Context, req *pb.SqlBackupRunsD
 		return nil, err
 	}
 
-	if err := s.storage.Delete(ctx, backupFqn, backupRun); err != nil {
+	// Cloud SQL keeps a deleted backup run: backupRuns.get still returns it,
+	// with status DELETED (seen against the real API, docs/live-runs.md in
+	// config-connector-extensions). Deleting it again is taken as not found.
+	if backupRun.Status == pb.SqlBackupRunStatus_DELETED {
+		return nil, status.Errorf(codes.NotFound, "The backup run does not exist.")
+	}
+	backupRun.Status = pb.SqlBackupRunStatus_DELETED
+	if err := s.storage.Update(ctx, backupFqn, backupRun); err != nil {
 		return nil, err
 	}
 
